{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "צפונה ונגבה וקדמה וימה", :translit "tzafonah u-negbah ve-kedmah ve-yamah", :gloss "northward and southward and eastward and westward"} {:he "ימה וקדמה וצפונה ונגבה", :translit "yamah u-kedmah u-tzafonah u-negbah", :gloss "westward and eastward and northward and southward"} {:he "שנשחטים בצפון", :translit "she-nishchatim ba-tzafon", :gloss "that are slaughtered in the north"} {:he "וירא ישראל את היד הגדולה", :translit "va-yar Yisra'el et ha-yad ha-gedolah", :gloss "And Israel saw the great hand"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word-order contrast between Genesis 13:14 (Abraham: north first) and Genesis 28:14 (Jacob: west first); each ordering carries symbolic significance."}], :frame {:text "The order of compass directions given to Abraham in Genesis 13:14 begins with north (tzafonah), while the order given to Jacob in Genesis 28:14 begins with west (yamah). Offerings of most holy sacrifices must be slaughtered in the north side of the altar, as stated in Leviticus 1:11, so God begins with north for Abraham to hint at the merit of those offerings. For Jacob, beginning with west (yamah, literally 'seaward') alludes to crossing the sea, recalling Exodus 14:31 where Israel sees God's great hand at the sea.", :sources ["Leviticus 1:11" "Genesis 28:14" "Exodus 14:31"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word-order contrast between Genesis 13:14 (Abraham: north first) and Genesis 28:14 (Jacob: west first); each ordering carries symbolic significance.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:05:41.216459382Z", :model "glm-5.2"}